// =============================================================================
//  probe_trade.hml — W7. A TRADE A PLAYER CAN COMPLETE, END TO END.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  The gate that produced this task measured, on a live session:
//
//      villagers show `[E] PIP / [T] TRADE`,  14 villagers,  5 named,
//      1 TRADE ATTEMPTED,  0 COMPLETED.
//
//  Everything downstream of that number — DIRECTION.md §3's weapon ladder,
//  §6's "the arsenal is a person", §7's carry capacity — was unreachable.
//  This probe is the regression test for the whole of it, and every assertion
//  below is one clause of the task:
//
//      open a trade . see what is offered and what it costs . pay for it .
//      carry it . be slowed by carrying it . put it back down in the world .
//      save it . load it . get the same answer twice from the same seed .
//
//  It drives `src/game/server.hml` with real `InputCommand`s and nothing else:
//  no client, no renderer, no SDL. `probe_game.hml`'s `nm | grep -c SDL_ == 0`
//  argument applies unchanged.
//
//  Run:  hemlockc -O1 tools/probe_trade.hml -o /tmp/pt && /tmp/pt
//  Exits 1 on any failure, and on an assertion COUNT that is not
//  `EXPECTED_ASSERTIONS` — a probe that silently stops running half its checks
//  is worse than one that fails.
// =============================================================================

